From: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: Give cross-compiling consumers a host-runnable flatc

The installed package config finds FlatBuffers for every consumer, and
HoloscanSchemaTools runs whatever flatbuffers::flatc names. In a cross
build that target comes from the target sysroot's FlatcTargets.cmake and
names the target-architecture flatc, so holoscan_add_flatbuffer_schema()
fails with an exec format error. Where a sysroot strips that export file,
the target is missing and the function stops at its own FATAL_ERROR.

When CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING, look for a flatc on the build host before
finding FlatBuffers and declare flatbuffers::flatc from it. The generated
FlatcTargets.cmake returns early when all of its targets already exist,
so the host binary is the one that stays. HOLOSCAN_FLATC_EXECUTABLE can
be set to choose it explicitly.

The search skips the package root and CMake prefix paths. By this point
holoscan-full-config.cmake has prepended the Holoscan install prefix, the
target sysroot's /usr, to CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH, and its bin/ holds the
target flatc. What is left is PATH and the system paths. Under an SDK
toolchain, which sets CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_PROGRAM to NEVER, that is
the SDK's host bin directory. Under an OpenEmbedded recipe build
(ONLY), it is the native sysroot. A target sysroot does not stage bin/.

Builds that are not cross-compiling are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Ilies CHERGUI <ichergui@nvidia.com>
---
diff --git a/cmake/templates/holoscan-config.cmake.in b/cmake/templates/holoscan-config.cmake.in
index 375de523e..adb4b276f 100644
--- a/cmake/templates/holoscan-config.cmake.in
+++ b/cmake/templates/holoscan-config.cmake.in
@@ -262,6 +262,20 @@ endif()
 unset(_holoscan_caller_transport_root)
 unset(_holoscan_caller_transport_root_defined)
 set(holoscan_FIND_COMPONENTS "${_holoscan_requested_components}")
+# A cross-compiled FlatBuffers package exports flatbuffers::flatc as its own
+# target-architecture binary, which the build host cannot run. Declare a flatc
+# the host can run first: FlatBuffers' export file then sees its only target
+# already defined and leaves it alone. The CMake prefix paths are skipped
+# because they hold the target install prefix.
+if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING AND NOT TARGET flatbuffers::flatc)
+  find_program(HOLOSCAN_FLATC_EXECUTABLE flatc
+    NO_PACKAGE_ROOT_PATH NO_CMAKE_PATH NO_CMAKE_ENVIRONMENT_PATH)
+  if(HOLOSCAN_FLATC_EXECUTABLE)
+    add_executable(flatbuffers::flatc IMPORTED)
+    set_target_properties(flatbuffers::flatc PROPERTIES
+      IMPORTED_LOCATION "${HOLOSCAN_FLATC_EXECUTABLE}")
+  endif()
+endif()
 find_dependency(Flatbuffers "@Flatbuffers_VERSION@" EXACT CONFIG
   HINTS "${_holoscan_frontdoor_install_prefix}/@HOLOSCAN_THIRD_PARTY_INSTALL_LIB_DIR@/cmake/flatbuffers")
 
